At the baseline value of 1 cent per point, 100 Chase Ultimate Rewards points equal $1.00, meaning 10,000 points are worth $100, 50,000 points are worth $500, and 100,000 points are worth $1,000. You also receive that same 1-cent rate when redeeming points for a statement credit through Pay Yourself Back toward eligible purchases from the prior 90 days. That dollar value rises only when you book travel through Points Boost or move points to airline and hotel transfer partners. On cards eligible for Points Boost, 50,000 points can reach $750 at 1.5 cents each or $1,000 at 2 cents each, while The Points Guy's June 2026 transfer partner benchmark of 2.05 cents values that same 50,000-point balance at $1,025.